WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:00.836
[ Watch on KissFlix.co ]

2
00:01.106 --> 00:03.442
[♪ theme song playing]

3
00:03.525 --> 00:04.651
PARK MINJAE'S LIST

4
00:04.735 --> 00:06.028
START DATING...

5
00:36.725 --> 00:41.063
BETWEEN STEPS

6
00:41.688 --> 00:43.940
CHARACTERS, PLACES, ORGANIZATIONS, AND EVENTS IN THIS DRAMA ARE FICTITIOUS

7
00:44.024 --> 00:45.651
THIS DRAMA CONTAINS SENSITIVE CONTENT

8
00:46.735 --> 00:48.945
EPISODE 10

9
00:49.029 --> 00:51.156
[siren wailing in distance]

10
00:56.787 --> 00:59.164
She said she suddenly couldn't breathe properly.

11
00:59.247 --> 01:01.083
That she's having trouble breathing.

12
01:01.166 --> 01:02.709
Was she in a car accident?

13
01:02.793 --> 01:05.045
No, not a car accident. It's just her breathing.

14
01:05.128 --> 01:07.172
Please fill out this registration form first.

15
01:09.466 --> 01:13.553
By any chance, did she mention having any chest pain?

16
01:15.180 --> 01:16.515
What kind of chest pain?

17
01:16.598 --> 01:18.558
Like a stabbing pain or something like that.

18
01:21.103 --> 01:22.104
Ah.

19
01:22.187 --> 01:23.563
-Excuse me for a second. -Okay.

20
01:28.151 --> 01:29.611
-I'm sorry. Just a second. -Sure.

21
01:29.695 --> 01:31.029
[line ringing]

22
01:33.657 --> 01:34.658
Yes, hello?

23
01:35.909 --> 01:37.160
Yeah, where are you now?

24
01:39.621 --> 01:40.622
What?

25
01:41.581 --> 01:42.582
[door opens]

26
01:43.708 --> 01:44.709
[door closes]

27
01:45.794 --> 01:46.795
[footsteps approaching]

28
02:11.570 --> 02:12.571
[Youjin sighs]

29
02:24.249 --> 02:25.625
Are you feeling better now?

30
02:29.504 --> 02:30.756
How's your breathing?

31
02:33.008 --> 02:35.802
Does your chest hurt or feel tight or anything?

32
02:37.679 --> 02:39.473
Yeah, I'm okay now.

33
02:40.474 --> 02:41.600
I feel better.

34
02:46.980 --> 02:47.981
I was praying.

35
02:50.942 --> 02:52.027
I said

36
02:53.612 --> 02:56.198
I was thankful that Minjae's surgery and chemo went well,

37
02:57.282 --> 02:59.034
and that he survived.

38
03:02.204 --> 03:04.331
And I prayed he'd stay healthy,

39
03:05.290 --> 03:07.709
just like he is now.

40
03:10.879 --> 03:12.005
And then...

41
03:14.341 --> 03:17.219
I prayed he'd meet someone better than me, someone good for him,

42
03:18.470 --> 03:20.847
and live a happy life with her.

43
03:25.227 --> 03:26.603
Is that all you prayed for?

44
03:28.813 --> 03:31.483
You didn't pray for Lee Jihoon's success or happiness?

45
03:33.443 --> 03:34.986
No, I didn't.

46
03:36.404 --> 03:37.447
That's stingy of you.

47
03:38.532 --> 03:40.742
You're not even a Christian anyway.

48
03:40.825 --> 03:43.411
Christian or not, I believe in God. I pray, too.

49
03:44.287 --> 03:45.580
What about you?

50
03:45.664 --> 03:47.415
You're not a Christian either.

51
03:50.460 --> 03:51.461
[Youjin sighs]

52
03:55.715 --> 03:58.885
Please keep our Professor Lee Jihoon healthy

53
03:58.969 --> 04:01.596
and let everything he does go smoothly.

54
04:01.680 --> 04:04.057
Just let everything work out for him, no matter what.

55
04:13.942 --> 04:18.196
Please keep Lim Youjin healthy and happy, too.

56
04:19.155 --> 04:24.578
I hope she'll never have to suffer heartbreak or get hurt again.

57
04:25.745 --> 04:26.746
And...

58
04:28.456 --> 04:31.126
I pray that she'll smile a lot more when she's with me.

59
04:31.209 --> 04:32.210
Amen.

60
04:37.883 --> 04:38.967
Amen!

61
04:39.050 --> 04:40.051
[chuckling] Gosh.

62
04:44.598 --> 04:46.308
Right.

63
04:48.560 --> 04:50.520
I didn't want to come empty-handed.

64
04:50.604 --> 04:52.522
Here's your Christmas present.

65
04:54.065 --> 04:56.026
[♪ light pleasant music playing]

66
04:56.109 --> 04:58.737
You said you got me something.

67
05:01.031 --> 05:03.408
Hey, sorry. I left it at... home.

68
05:05.076 --> 05:06.077
Hmm.

69
05:06.369 --> 05:07.704
Did you buy this for me?

70
05:11.082 --> 05:12.083
Hey, give me that.

71
05:12.167 --> 05:13.168
Oh, oh, oh.

72
05:16.129 --> 05:20.091
Fine. It's a special occasion, so... here.

73
05:21.509 --> 05:22.969
-What is it? -Guess.

74
05:25.263 --> 05:26.556
What is it? Is it expensive?

75
05:27.474 --> 05:29.434
Well, it's kind of expensive.

76
05:32.479 --> 05:33.647
It's yellow.

77
05:34.522 --> 05:35.607
[in English] Yellow?

78
05:37.275 --> 05:38.526
-Yellow? -[in Korean] Yeah.

79
05:40.111 --> 05:41.404
And it's sparkly.

80
05:42.364 --> 05:43.615
-Yellow and sparkly. -Yeah.

81
05:45.450 --> 05:46.451
[in English] Gold?

82
05:47.535 --> 05:48.536
[scoffs]

83
05:49.037 --> 05:51.414
[in Korean] You know how expensive gold is these days.

84
05:52.749 --> 05:53.750
Thank you.

85
05:54.376 --> 05:55.377
Thanks.

86
05:57.337 --> 05:58.338
[giggling]

87
05:58.421 --> 06:00.423
I made them.

88
06:00.507 --> 06:01.675
Sparkly.

89
06:03.969 --> 06:04.970
Hmm.

90
06:05.637 --> 06:09.015
It's not store-bought. It's handmade.

91
06:09.099 --> 06:10.100
Yeah.

92
06:11.267 --> 06:14.938
Didn't you have black yarn or anything?

93
06:15.522 --> 06:17.565
Hmm... There was no black yarn.

94
06:18.608 --> 06:20.944
This was the only lambswool yarn I had left at home.

95
06:21.027 --> 06:22.195
You could've bought some.

96
06:22.278 --> 06:25.073
I could have. But I was too busy to go buy any.

97
06:26.282 --> 06:28.034
Aren't they cute, though?

98
06:30.286 --> 06:32.080
And what did you get for me?

99
06:32.163 --> 06:34.249
If it's not chocolate, what did you get?

100
06:38.503 --> 06:39.838
I didn't get you anything.

101
06:42.549 --> 06:45.218
I lied. I didn't get you anything. So take these back.

102
06:50.306 --> 06:51.850
I'm hungry.

103
06:51.933 --> 06:53.268
Want to have some ramyeon?

104
07:07.699 --> 07:09.701
[♪ somber music playing]

105
07:31.723 --> 07:32.724
[sighs]

106
07:59.834 --> 08:00.835
[sighs]

107
08:03.296 --> 08:05.924
-[♪ lively music playing over speakers] -[staff] Welcome.

108
08:07.217 --> 08:08.593
[woman] Dajeong! Over here.

109
08:16.559 --> 08:18.061
Look at the shrimp and abalone.

110
08:19.896 --> 08:21.064
It's good here, isn't it?

111
08:22.398 --> 08:23.691
Yeah.

112
08:23.775 --> 08:25.902
This is my secret spot, so keep it to yourself.

113
08:28.363 --> 08:29.364
[sighs]

114
08:32.283 --> 08:33.284
What?

115
08:36.162 --> 08:37.747
What do you think he was thinking?

116
08:39.040 --> 08:40.041
Huh?

117
08:41.417 --> 08:42.836
Because of me,

118
08:43.419 --> 08:45.046
because he didn't want me to worry,

119
08:45.755 --> 08:48.508
he broke up with me without even telling me he was sick.

120
08:48.591 --> 08:50.051
Does that make any sense to you?

121
08:50.135 --> 08:52.137
It just sounds like bullshit to me.

122
08:52.220 --> 08:54.305
-Right? It's bullshit. -Yeah.

123
08:55.098 --> 08:56.182
[exclaims]

124
08:56.266 --> 08:58.017
And then he had the nerve to tell me...

125
08:59.352 --> 09:01.229
He told me to let it all out,

126
09:01.312 --> 09:03.648
and live happily ever after with my husband.

127
09:03.731 --> 09:05.066
That's bullshit too.

128
09:05.150 --> 09:06.151
[Youjin] Yeah.

129
09:08.736 --> 09:09.904
It's a little spicy.

130
09:10.572 --> 09:11.573
Can I get a beer...

131
09:12.907 --> 09:13.908
Me too.

132
09:16.286 --> 09:18.037
What do you want? Beer or highball?

133
09:18.121 --> 09:19.164
Either one.

134
09:19.247 --> 09:20.290
-[phone vibrating] -Then beer.

135
09:24.961 --> 09:26.963
[bell rings, musical chime]

136
09:29.048 --> 09:30.049
Hello?

137
09:31.843 --> 09:32.844
Hello?

138
09:35.388 --> 09:36.472
Hello?

139
09:37.390 --> 09:39.851
Who are you? Say something.

140
09:42.061 --> 09:45.732
I think you have the wrong number. If you're not going to talk, I'll hang up.

141
09:45.815 --> 09:47.609
Hey, it's me.

142
09:48.318 --> 09:49.569
It's Park Minjae.

143
09:54.949 --> 09:58.995
Well, I was wondering if you got home okay or if something happened.

144
09:59.078 --> 10:00.288
I was worried.

145
10:01.581 --> 10:03.041
[Jihoon] Who's that? Who's calling?

146
10:07.086 --> 10:10.465
I can't really talk right now. Next time...

147
10:12.050 --> 10:13.051
I've got to go.

148
10:14.677 --> 10:15.678
[line disconnects]

149
10:18.556 --> 10:20.558
[♪ somber music playing]

150
10:22.477 --> 10:23.811
[sighs]

151
10:35.156 --> 10:36.199
[sighs]

152
10:50.546 --> 10:51.547
[sighs]

153
10:55.385 --> 10:57.804
[bell tolling in distance]

154
11:14.445 --> 11:15.488
Thank you.

155
11:44.434 --> 11:45.435
Aren't you going in?

156
11:49.689 --> 11:50.898
Aren't you going to go in?

157
11:54.861 --> 11:55.862
It's cold.

158
12:04.537 --> 12:06.748
Why are you holding my hand without asking?

159
12:06.831 --> 12:07.915
Why not?

160
12:07.999 --> 12:09.167
What's the big deal?

161
12:09.667 --> 12:11.336
What's wrong with holding your hand?

162
12:11.419 --> 12:13.379
Your hand is so cold, you can't feel a thing.

163
12:16.090 --> 12:18.968
You barely had any beer, and you're acting like a total drunk.

164
12:19.052 --> 12:20.887
I'm never going to drink with you again.

165
12:21.429 --> 12:23.348
I'm not acting like a drunk. I'm not drunk.

166
12:23.431 --> 12:24.432
Then what is it?

167
12:27.435 --> 12:28.770
Is it because of Park Minjae?

168
12:31.773 --> 12:34.275
If you can't get over him and you like him that much,

169
12:34.359 --> 12:35.943
then get back together with him.

170
12:40.740 --> 12:42.033
Don't you start crying here.

171
12:43.117 --> 12:44.285
Don't you dare.

172
12:49.582 --> 12:50.666
Do whatever you want.

173
12:58.007 --> 12:59.008
Give me those.

174
13:00.885 --> 13:03.262
Give me those silly yellow gloves. They're mine.

175
13:11.646 --> 13:12.980
[muttering] What's wrong with him?

176
13:15.441 --> 13:16.651
[Jihoon sighs]

177
13:26.619 --> 13:27.829
If I...

178
13:30.957 --> 13:32.750
If I asked you out, would you say yes?

179
13:34.627 --> 13:35.837
What?

180
13:38.172 --> 13:39.674
I did get you a gift.

181
13:40.633 --> 13:41.634
A bracelet.

182
13:43.344 --> 13:45.721
It's real gold, not gold-plated or anything.

183
13:48.558 --> 13:49.684
Because it was pretty.

184
13:51.060 --> 13:52.979
The second I saw it, I thought of you.

185
13:53.062 --> 13:55.064
So I bought it without a second thought.

186
13:57.984 --> 13:59.777
If I give you that and ask you out,

187
14:01.946 --> 14:03.156
will you accept it?

188
14:08.035 --> 14:09.537
What are you going to do?

189
14:12.456 --> 14:13.624
What's your answer?

190
14:18.337 --> 14:19.505
I'm not sure

191
14:21.257 --> 14:22.842
what you're talking about.

192
14:27.305 --> 14:28.306
Fine.

193
14:30.099 --> 14:31.392
You wait right here.

194
15:06.219 --> 15:07.803
MOM AND DAD ARE GOING TO HONGCHEON

195
15:07.887 --> 15:09.805
THERE'S CURRY IN THE POT, SO HELP YOURSELF

196
15:09.889 --> 15:11.098
AND DON'T FIGHT, YOU TWO!

197
15:12.016 --> 15:13.601
What does he even mean?

198
15:15.144 --> 15:16.604
What am I supposed to do?

199
15:19.982 --> 15:20.983
[sighs]

200
15:57.019 --> 15:58.896
[sighs]

201
15:58.980 --> 16:02.817
LIM YOUJIN MOBILE 010-0646-7905

202
16:03.734 --> 16:04.986
[sighs]

203
16:07.571 --> 16:09.073
[sighs]

204
16:14.203 --> 16:15.204
[sighs]

205
16:22.545 --> 16:25.214
Subin! Subin!

206
16:25.298 --> 16:27.717
-Subin! Here. Over here. -Oh!

207
16:32.430 --> 16:33.889
Sorry, I'm late.

208
16:33.973 --> 16:37.184
No, you're not late at all. The bus isn't even here.

209
16:37.268 --> 16:38.477
Ah...

210
16:39.645 --> 16:40.646
Oh, right.

211
16:45.067 --> 16:46.068
Merry Christmas.

212
16:48.612 --> 16:49.822
Merry Christmas.

213
16:53.993 --> 16:55.119
Give me the bag.

214
16:55.202 --> 16:57.204
What? No, I'm fine.

215
17:02.335 --> 17:03.336
[chuckles softly]

216
17:06.630 --> 17:07.631
[Sejin clears throat]

217
17:09.425 --> 17:10.426
Oh.

218
17:10.509 --> 17:12.970
Is that your snowboard?

219
17:13.971 --> 17:15.848
Ah. Yes.

220
17:16.932 --> 17:18.184
That's cool.

221
17:20.061 --> 17:22.563
Uh, it's not expensive or anything.

222
17:22.646 --> 17:24.815
I just have one because I like snowboarding.

223
17:26.150 --> 17:27.193
It's cool.

224
17:28.069 --> 17:29.570
This... It's not hard at all.

225
17:29.654 --> 17:31.781
You'll pick it up in no time. I can teach you.

226
17:31.864 --> 17:32.865
Okay.

227
17:40.915 --> 17:43.209
-Put this in your pocket. -[chuckles]

228
17:43.876 --> 17:44.877
Thank you.

229
17:47.672 --> 17:49.006
[phone vibrating]

230
17:51.050 --> 17:52.093
One second.

231
17:52.176 --> 17:53.177
Okay.

232
17:55.012 --> 17:56.639
Yes, hello?

233
17:56.722 --> 17:57.723
Yes.

234
18:01.519 --> 18:02.645
Yes.

235
18:05.314 --> 18:06.357
Minjae!

236
18:08.067 --> 18:09.193
Have you been well?

237
18:11.070 --> 18:13.906
Yeah. Me too.

238
18:16.617 --> 18:18.703
Well, I've been busy.

239
18:18.786 --> 18:20.204
Just frantic.

240
18:20.746 --> 18:21.747
Yeah.

241
18:21.831 --> 18:22.832
Okay.

242
18:24.917 --> 18:25.918
Yeah.

243
18:27.461 --> 18:29.046
Of course. Yeah.

244
18:38.097 --> 18:40.099
Tomorrow?

245
18:43.853 --> 18:44.854
You're busy?

246
18:46.355 --> 18:50.109
If you're busy, don't worry about it.

247
18:50.192 --> 18:51.193
Yeah.

248
18:51.277 --> 18:53.070
Okay, then let's meet up with everyone.

249
18:53.154 --> 18:54.822
We can just meet all together. Yeah.

250
18:56.240 --> 18:57.241
Okay.

251
18:58.367 --> 18:59.368
-Sejin. -Yeah.

252
18:59.452 --> 19:00.536
The bus is here.

253
19:02.872 --> 19:04.081
All right.

254
19:10.546 --> 19:12.548
[♪ intriguing music playing]

255
19:14.300 --> 19:15.593
This is the bus, right?

256
19:30.858 --> 19:32.318
Should we put it in here?

257
19:34.195 --> 19:35.196
Yeah.

258
19:42.161 --> 19:43.162
[chuckles]

259
19:48.000 --> 19:49.168
Here's the ticket.

260
19:55.841 --> 19:56.842
-Um... -Oh?

261
19:58.511 --> 20:00.137
-Subin. -Yes?

262
20:00.221 --> 20:01.597
I'll take this one with me.

263
20:05.309 --> 20:06.310
Uh...

264
20:10.439 --> 20:11.482
I'm afraid...

265
20:15.986 --> 20:17.863
I won't be able to go with you today.

266
20:19.365 --> 20:20.366
What?

267
20:20.449 --> 20:22.451
[♪ glum music playing]

268
20:23.661 --> 20:24.787
I'm sorry.

269
20:31.544 --> 20:33.337
[sighs]

270
20:35.256 --> 20:36.632
[knocking at window]

271
20:38.634 --> 20:41.554
Call me when you get there.

272
21:37.276 --> 21:39.403
[♪ lively music playing over speakers]

273
21:46.952 --> 21:47.953
Hey.

274
21:50.039 --> 21:51.957
It's been a while. Right?

275
21:53.709 --> 21:54.710
-Minjae. -[chuckles]

276
21:54.793 --> 21:56.962
Oh, man. Okay.

277
21:58.881 --> 21:59.882
Let's go.

278
22:02.301 --> 22:04.678
Come on. Stop.

279
22:04.762 --> 22:05.804
[straining] Let go.

280
22:06.347 --> 22:07.806
I said let go, you freaking...

281
22:10.392 --> 22:11.393
You.

282
22:12.394 --> 22:14.355
Hey, it's been so long. Right?

283
22:14.438 --> 22:16.273
How long has it been?

284
22:16.357 --> 22:18.734
I'm sorry I haven't been in touch.

285
22:19.985 --> 22:21.570
I heard you were sick.

286
22:23.280 --> 22:24.406
How did you know?

287
22:24.490 --> 22:26.909
I overheard Professor Ahn on the phone.

288
22:28.118 --> 22:29.119
Oh.

289
22:30.079 --> 22:31.538
Are you all better now?

290
22:32.831 --> 22:35.751
I'm fine. The surgery went well.

291
22:35.834 --> 22:36.835
I'm fine.

292
22:38.003 --> 22:39.213
[sighs]

293
22:39.296 --> 22:41.173
How about you? How have you been?

294
22:42.299 --> 22:44.593
Well, I was just... I was doing fine.

295
22:44.677 --> 22:46.762
Going to school, studying...

296
22:48.681 --> 22:49.848
How about a girlfriend?

297
22:52.768 --> 22:56.647
You said you liked that, you know, Jung Subin girl.

298
22:56.730 --> 22:59.066
You said she was beautiful, like an angel.

299
22:59.149 --> 23:01.276
Are you guys still in the talking stage?

300
23:01.360 --> 23:04.530
We're not in any stage. We're just friends. She's a female friend.

301
23:04.613 --> 23:06.323
Friends? You've got to be kidding me.

302
23:06.407 --> 23:08.701
Hey, after all the support I'd given you,

303
23:08.784 --> 23:11.537
there should've been some progress, some results.

304
23:12.037 --> 23:13.414
No, there's really nothing.

305
23:15.499 --> 23:16.750
[chuckling]

306
23:19.712 --> 23:22.423
How about Youjin? Is she doing well?

307
23:24.299 --> 23:25.509
Well...

308
23:25.592 --> 23:29.263
I heard she was getting married soon.

309
23:29.888 --> 23:31.098
[yelling] She's getting married?

310
23:34.518 --> 23:35.602
She's not?

311
23:36.103 --> 23:37.312
Was I mistaken?

312
23:38.939 --> 23:39.940
Well,

313
23:40.941 --> 23:42.151
not quite marriage.

314
23:43.736 --> 23:44.945
But she's seeing someone.

315
23:46.238 --> 23:47.239
Oh.

316
23:47.698 --> 23:49.533
You know Professor Lee Jihoon from math?

317
23:49.616 --> 23:51.201
I heard they're seeing each other.

318
23:51.285 --> 23:53.662
But marriage...

319
23:53.746 --> 23:55.581
I don't think they're quite there yet.

320
23:56.832 --> 24:00.461
Well, if they keep seeing each other, they'll eventually get married.

321
24:01.879 --> 24:05.674
But Professor Lee Jihoon is an alpha, you know.

322
24:06.633 --> 24:07.676
Alpha?

323
24:07.760 --> 24:11.013
I mean, he has a strong personality. He's assertive and kind of prickly.

324
24:13.599 --> 24:17.311
Yeah. He's not exactly the easiest person to deal with.

325
24:17.895 --> 24:21.190
But apparently, he's popular with girls.

326
24:22.024 --> 24:23.025
They say he's sexy.

327
24:24.568 --> 24:25.861
He's sexy?

328
24:26.612 --> 24:28.530
What's so sexy about him?

329
24:28.614 --> 24:29.615
I'm not sure.

330
24:30.616 --> 24:34.912
Women are attracted to intellectual and smart men, you know.

331
24:34.995 --> 24:36.663
Maybe it's that kind of sexiness?

332
24:36.747 --> 24:37.748
[scoffs]

333
24:39.541 --> 24:42.503
I'm like that myself, so I kind of get the appeal.

334
24:43.253 --> 24:44.505
Ah.

335
24:44.588 --> 24:45.798
That's right.

336
24:46.465 --> 24:49.176
Yeah, he is sexy.

337
24:49.843 --> 24:51.720
I can see why women feel that way.

338
24:55.599 --> 25:01.313
Anyway, people like him have high standards for others too.

339
25:02.314 --> 25:05.150
Honestly, I don't get how Lim Youjin meets his standards...

340
25:05.234 --> 25:06.235
[sucks teeth]

341
25:06.318 --> 25:09.029
She's not even that pretty, and she has a weird personality.

342
25:09.113 --> 25:12.366
She's also dumb and stubborn. There's nothing appealing about her.

343
25:12.449 --> 25:14.118
[sighs deeply]

344
25:14.201 --> 25:17.079
Honestly, I don't even get why you dated her.

345
25:17.162 --> 25:18.580
It's all over now, though.

346
25:24.545 --> 25:25.712
Have you...

347
25:27.464 --> 25:29.883
told anyone about me and Youjin dating, by any chance?

348
25:29.967 --> 25:30.968
What?

349
25:31.468 --> 25:33.595
No. I didn't tell anyone.

350
25:33.679 --> 25:36.056
Why would I talk about that? It's your personal life.

351
25:37.057 --> 25:38.183
[Sejin clears throat]

352
25:38.976 --> 25:41.353
[sighs] But why...

353
25:42.604 --> 25:44.523
And talking about that

354
25:44.606 --> 25:47.192
would put Lim Youjin in an awkward position.

355
25:47.943 --> 25:50.988
Who would want a woman with a past?

356
25:51.780 --> 25:52.990
A past?

357
25:53.073 --> 25:55.159
How is Youjin a woman with a past?

358
25:55.242 --> 26:00.164
Well, men don't want to know about their girlfriend's exes, you know.

359
26:00.247 --> 26:02.207
It's kind of off-putting, to be honest.

360
26:03.792 --> 26:06.295
Even just hearing about it feels bad enough.

361
26:06.378 --> 26:08.005
But seeing the guy in front of you?

362
26:08.088 --> 26:09.715
[sighs] That'd be seriously annoying.

363
26:11.175 --> 26:14.553
You start hounding her, getting suspicious, keeping tabs on her.

364
26:14.636 --> 26:16.513
Then you start suspecting she's cheating.

365
26:17.598 --> 26:19.391
Come on, that's what a psycho would do.

366
26:19.474 --> 26:22.269
Minjae, there are so many psychos in this country.

367
26:23.937 --> 26:26.857
[sighs] There are nutjobs everywhere.

368
26:33.113 --> 26:36.491
Is that why he suggested the three of us meet up?

369
26:37.159 --> 26:38.160
What?

370
26:38.243 --> 26:42.623
So, he invited me to see how I'd react.

371
26:44.750 --> 26:46.919
Wow, what a psycho.

372
27:06.897 --> 27:07.898
[box slams shut]

373
27:44.226 --> 27:45.227
[sighs]

374
27:45.727 --> 27:47.020
[phone vibrating]

375
27:57.823 --> 27:59.825
[♪ jazz music playing over speakers]

376
28:07.165 --> 28:08.375
-Hey. -Hello.

377
28:11.670 --> 28:12.754
Have a seat.

378
28:17.050 --> 28:18.719
Hey, can you drink? You have cancer.

379
28:19.594 --> 28:20.595
Oh...

380
28:21.596 --> 28:23.473
Well. Suit yourself.

381
28:23.557 --> 28:25.017
Can I get another glass, please?

382
28:25.642 --> 28:26.643
Sure thing.

383
28:27.519 --> 28:29.563
So, what is it you wanted to tell me?

384
28:31.481 --> 28:33.275
You said it was important.

385
28:36.737 --> 28:37.738
[staff] Here.

386
28:38.697 --> 28:39.823
-Thank you. -[staff] Enjoy.

387
28:42.117 --> 28:43.493
Whatever it is, shoot.

388
28:52.669 --> 28:54.629
I'd like to know your intentions, Professor.

389
28:55.172 --> 28:56.173
What intentions?

390
28:58.175 --> 29:00.677
That day, why did you suddenly...

391
29:00.761 --> 29:03.055
Wait, that thing on your face.

392
29:03.138 --> 29:05.182
On the right side. Is that a dimple?

393
29:05.265 --> 29:06.266
Pardon?

394
29:06.892 --> 29:08.810
[Jihoon] When you smile. Yeah, there it is.

395
29:08.894 --> 29:10.771
-This... -Is it a dimple, not a wrinkle?

396
29:11.563 --> 29:12.647
Yes.

397
29:14.566 --> 29:16.151
I have dimples too.

398
29:22.115 --> 29:24.618
It's not like you're insanely good-looking or anything.

399
29:25.243 --> 29:27.496
Definitely not something you can't get over.

400
29:29.956 --> 29:31.833
I heard you told Youjin

401
29:31.917 --> 29:33.627
to get over you

402
29:33.710 --> 29:35.712
and move on to someone better.

403
29:39.257 --> 29:42.010
She's trying so hard to move on and build a happy life.

404
29:42.094 --> 29:44.513
Why did you come back? What are you still hung up on?

405
29:46.556 --> 29:48.475
I think there's a misunderstanding here.

406
29:48.558 --> 29:52.646
Why? Is it hard to accept that things between you two ended just like that?

407
29:53.230 --> 29:55.690
You just can't seem to move on?

408
29:57.109 --> 29:59.820
I'm not back because I haven't moved on.

409
29:59.903 --> 30:02.614
I mean, you're the one who broke up with her.

410
30:02.697 --> 30:03.824
Right?

411
30:03.907 --> 30:05.158
So just fuck off.

412
30:06.660 --> 30:09.955
It's true that I'm the one who broke up with her.

413
30:10.038 --> 30:13.583
But if you just tell me to fuck off without knowing the situation,

414
30:14.334 --> 30:16.294
I've got a few things to say too...

415
30:18.588 --> 30:21.007
Situation, my ass. That's just bullshit.

416
30:21.091 --> 30:23.009
Want me to say what you're really thinking?

417
30:25.053 --> 30:27.097
What was I really thinking?

418
30:27.180 --> 30:28.473
You were confident.

419
30:29.724 --> 30:33.061
The moment you broke up with her, and even now.

420
30:33.145 --> 30:36.106
Confident... What am I confident about?

421
30:37.065 --> 30:39.776
You think you can go back to how things were.

422
30:44.447 --> 30:46.366
Honestly, a loser like you? I thought...

423
30:48.118 --> 30:49.619
Yeah.

424
30:49.703 --> 30:51.413
I definitely underestimated you.

425
30:53.832 --> 30:55.417
But it only took you five minutes.

426
30:57.502 --> 30:59.629
Man, you didn't even have to see her.

427
30:59.713 --> 31:02.674
One phone call with you, and she just crumbled.

428
31:05.635 --> 31:06.636
You arrogant,

429
31:07.721 --> 31:09.014
proud,

430
31:09.764 --> 31:11.016
entitled asshole.

431
31:14.853 --> 31:16.313
But it's not going to happen.

432
31:17.772 --> 31:18.982
Because she has me.

433
31:20.775 --> 31:23.236
It won't happen. It's too late.

434
31:25.655 --> 31:27.949
What if I had died?

435
31:29.451 --> 31:31.328
What if I had died?

436
31:34.998 --> 31:36.750
Think about it.

437
31:36.833 --> 31:39.753
If I had died, what would that have done to her?

438
31:41.630 --> 31:45.926
It was better to hurt her a little now than hurt her even more later. Am I wrong?

439
31:48.845 --> 31:50.680
This...

440
31:50.764 --> 31:52.766
This is unfair to me too. I...

441
31:52.849 --> 31:54.476
It's not fair to me.

442
31:58.813 --> 32:01.024
You're a real piece of work, aren't you?

443
32:02.609 --> 32:05.320
Hey, are any of us gods here?

444
32:06.238 --> 32:07.781
Aren't we all just human?

445
32:08.782 --> 32:11.326
Fuck all that bullshit. You like someone, you date them.

446
32:11.409 --> 32:14.162
It doesn't work out, you break up. That's it.

447
32:14.246 --> 32:16.581
It's as simple as that. How are you the victim here?

448
32:17.624 --> 32:19.292
[♪ emotional song playing]

449
32:19.376 --> 32:20.377
Whatever.

450
32:21.044 --> 32:22.671
You had your chance, and it's over.

451
32:23.755 --> 32:25.715
So stop playing with Youjin's feelings.

452
32:29.970 --> 32:31.179
You know what?

453
32:32.973 --> 32:35.100
You never know what life might throw at us.

454
32:36.434 --> 32:39.562
Watch out for cars. There are a lot of car accidents out there.

455
32:41.856 --> 32:43.191
Stay alive.

456
33:07.966 --> 33:10.176
[door lock beeps]

457
33:17.726 --> 33:19.185
[door lock chimes]

458
34:19.371 --> 34:20.372
[sighs]

459
34:35.970 --> 34:36.971
[exhales]

460
34:46.314 --> 34:47.315
[sighs]

461
34:49.025 --> 34:50.193
[groans softly]

462
35:00.537 --> 35:01.538
[sighs]

463
35:06.126 --> 35:07.127
[sighs]

464
35:33.445 --> 35:34.446
[♪ music fades]

465
35:37.407 --> 35:40.577
[Miyoung] That's a lot of sesame seeds.

466
35:41.411 --> 35:43.455
It's not sesame seeds, it's sesame oil.

467
35:43.538 --> 35:46.291
Yeah, this is it. Authentic sesame oil made in Korea.

468
35:46.374 --> 35:48.251
Was there a lot of snow in Hongcheon?

469
35:48.334 --> 35:50.587
[groans] Tons of snow.

470
35:50.670 --> 35:53.798
And with holiday traffic, the roads were so backed up. It was awful.

471
35:53.882 --> 35:55.008
-Mom. -Yeah?

472
35:55.091 --> 35:57.218
Didn't Grandma ask why I didn't come?

473
35:57.302 --> 35:59.929
She did. She said she wanted to see you.

474
36:00.764 --> 36:04.434
That was it? Didn't she tell you to give me some money or anything?

475
36:04.517 --> 36:07.228
[Miyoung] Jeez, you should be the one giving her money.

476
36:07.312 --> 36:08.730
[Youjin] I know. So immature.

477
36:08.813 --> 36:10.815
-[Miyoung sighs, groans] -[Youjin grunts]

478
36:10.899 --> 36:11.983
Youjin,

479
36:12.484 --> 36:15.528
you know your great-aunt in Hongcheon, right?

480
36:15.612 --> 36:18.281
That great-aunt's sister-in-law's father-in-law...

481
36:18.364 --> 36:20.158
No, that's not it.

482
36:20.241 --> 36:23.119
The sister-in-law's husband's older brother.

483
36:23.203 --> 36:25.246
Honey, what does that make him to us?

484
36:25.872 --> 36:30.710
Wouldn't that make him our in-law's in-law? No?

485
36:30.794 --> 36:31.795
I don't know.

486
36:31.878 --> 36:37.133
Anyway, that in-law's in-law is super rich and owns a bunch of buildings.

487
36:37.217 --> 36:39.385
One of the buildings is an assemblyman's office,

488
36:39.469 --> 36:41.805
so they're pretty close with the assemblyman too.

489
36:41.888 --> 36:44.724
Apparently, that assemblyman's son is your alum.

490
36:45.266 --> 36:47.018
He studied economics at Seohan.

491
36:47.977 --> 36:49.187
And he's 32.

492
36:49.270 --> 36:51.940
He's a Deputy Director at the MOFE. What do you think?

493
36:53.066 --> 36:54.317
What do you mean?

494
36:54.859 --> 36:57.946
He's still just a civil servant. That's not exactly a great catch.

495
36:58.988 --> 37:01.491
A Deputy Director is a Grade 5 official.

496
37:01.574 --> 37:04.077
He's not just any government worker. He's a bureaucrat.

497
37:04.160 --> 37:06.037
Right. He's a high-ranking bureaucrat.

498
37:06.120 --> 37:09.165
But if he's a politician's son and a high-ranking bureaucrat,

499
37:09.249 --> 37:11.209
he must have plenty of good matches. Why us?

500
37:11.835 --> 37:13.837
He's picky.

501
37:13.920 --> 37:16.506
No school bullying in the past, no tax issues.

502
37:16.589 --> 37:19.634
And most importantly, he wants someone pretty.

503
37:19.717 --> 37:21.177
He says she can't be ugly.

504
37:22.011 --> 37:23.763
-And that's her? -Hey.

505
37:23.847 --> 37:25.807
You should show him her bare face.

506
37:25.890 --> 37:28.184
What do you say? Do you want to meet him?

507
37:28.268 --> 37:30.103
No. I'm busy. I can't.

508
37:30.186 --> 37:32.313
Come on. Just meet up with him once.

509
37:32.856 --> 37:33.857
No.

510
37:33.940 --> 37:35.483
I knew you'd say that.

511
37:36.276 --> 37:39.529
Then do you have any friends you could introduce him to?

512
37:39.612 --> 37:41.823
He's a really good catch.

513
37:44.409 --> 37:45.577
Hmm...

514
37:46.327 --> 37:47.453
How about Subin?

515
37:48.413 --> 37:49.539
Well, Subin is pretty.

516
37:49.622 --> 37:52.166
She's kind and well-behaved. She also went to Seohan.

517
37:53.042 --> 37:55.003
Well, I don't know about Subin.

518
37:55.086 --> 37:56.087
Why not?

519
37:57.797 --> 37:59.591
Well, to be honest,

520
38:01.050 --> 38:04.095
I've always wanted her to be our daughter-in-law.

521
38:04.762 --> 38:05.763
[Youjin] What?

522
38:05.847 --> 38:08.057
-What? Me? -[Youjin laughing]

523
38:08.141 --> 38:09.767
No way.

524
38:13.605 --> 38:16.274
Come on. You're being ridiculous now.

525
38:18.526 --> 38:19.986
Yeah, I know.

526
38:20.069 --> 38:21.654
I know it's ridiculous.

527
38:23.031 --> 38:24.699
Well, it's just wishful thinking.

528
38:27.952 --> 38:30.914
Well. If only Youseong had gone to a university in Seoul,

529
38:30.997 --> 38:33.541
I would've done whatever it took to make it work.

530
38:34.250 --> 38:35.251
What?

531
38:35.335 --> 38:39.380
Well, Youseong could always go to college later.

532
38:40.590 --> 38:43.259
He's got a good personality.

533
38:43.343 --> 38:44.886
And he's good-looking too.

534
38:46.346 --> 38:48.890
Even if he has a good personality and is good-looking,

535
38:48.973 --> 38:50.850
his academic background isn't good enough.

536
38:51.476 --> 38:53.770
Her parents wouldn't like it.

537
38:53.853 --> 38:55.980
A good personality and good-looking? Who?

538
38:58.399 --> 39:00.193
His background aside,

539
39:00.276 --> 39:03.154
Subin gets along with Youseong just fine.

540
39:04.739 --> 39:06.491
And they're close too.

541
39:06.991 --> 39:09.118
I mean, as long as they like each other, right?

542
39:09.744 --> 39:12.121
It just doesn't work like that in real life.

543
39:12.622 --> 39:13.873
Stop.

544
39:14.916 --> 39:18.294
Subin is just like a little sister to me. I don't see her that way.

545
39:18.378 --> 39:19.462
She isn't even my type.

546
39:19.545 --> 39:23.299
[sighs] That's enough. You guys are just talking nonsense.

547
39:27.887 --> 39:28.888
[Miyoung] Gosh.

548
39:30.807 --> 39:34.268
This is why you should've studied hard, like I told you to.

549
39:34.352 --> 39:35.478
Stop it.

550
39:35.561 --> 39:38.356
I said I'm not interested in Subin. Why keep bringing it up?

551
39:41.859 --> 39:42.860
Jeez.

552
39:55.873 --> 39:57.875
[♪ theme song playing]

553
40:35.788 --> 40:42.503
[automated voice] The 650 bus and the 5533 bus will be arriving shortly.

554
40:44.672 --> 40:46.007
-Hey. -Jesus Christ!

555
40:46.090 --> 40:47.175
[laughs]

556
40:48.634 --> 40:49.635
Minjae!

557
40:51.596 --> 40:53.598
You haven't officially started yet, have you?

558
40:53.723 --> 40:56.768
I still need to go clean things up and get everything ready.

559
40:58.061 --> 41:00.813
Are you going to be taking the shuttle bus to work?

560
41:00.897 --> 41:03.399
I think so. That's probably what I'll do.

561
41:04.692 --> 41:06.152
Aren't you going to buy a car?

562
41:06.235 --> 41:08.237
No, driving around would be more of a hassle.

563
41:08.988 --> 41:11.074
But you're a professor. You should have a car.

564
41:11.157 --> 41:13.034
I'm not a professor.

565
41:13.117 --> 41:14.202
You are, though.

566
41:15.244 --> 41:16.287
-It's here. -It's here.

567
41:17.538 --> 41:18.831
Get in. Yeah, let's go.

568
41:18.915 --> 41:20.625
-It's a bit cold today. -Yeah.

569
41:32.303 --> 41:33.721
[Minjae] Hey, come on. Just sit there.

570
41:33.805 --> 41:35.515
You always do this.

571
41:36.557 --> 41:38.142
-Subin. -Hello.

572
41:38.226 --> 41:40.645
-It's been a while, right? -[Subin] Yeah.

573
41:40.728 --> 41:42.438
Hello.

574
41:42.522 --> 41:44.565
-I heard you were back. -Yeah.

575
41:53.449 --> 41:55.451
[inaudible conversation]

576
42:14.804 --> 42:17.140
See you around, Subin. I'll keep in touch.

577
42:44.041 --> 42:45.042
[♪ music fades]

578
42:45.126 --> 42:47.712
It's been so long since I've been back on campus,

579
42:47.795 --> 42:49.714
but it looks like it hasn't changed much.

580
42:49.797 --> 42:52.508
The buses, the roads, the field...

581
42:52.592 --> 42:54.468
Everything's just the same.

582
42:55.636 --> 42:57.263
And you haven't changed, either.

583
42:57.346 --> 43:00.558
You said you'd become a better person by the time I got back.

584
43:00.641 --> 43:02.935
You don't seem all that different to me.

585
43:08.816 --> 43:10.443
Well, that's what you said then.

586
43:11.444 --> 43:13.362
Why are you bringing that up now?

587
43:14.488 --> 43:16.991
It's pointless and not funny. What do you want?

588
43:19.118 --> 43:20.369
I mean...

589
43:21.078 --> 43:23.080
We can't stay like this forever, you know.

590
43:25.791 --> 43:26.792
[sighs]

591
43:28.336 --> 43:29.462
I messed up.

592
43:30.713 --> 43:32.840
I know I messed up too.

593
43:33.883 --> 43:34.884
So...

594
43:37.637 --> 43:38.971
Please forgive me.

595
43:40.514 --> 43:42.892
Okay, I forgive you.

596
43:43.976 --> 43:46.145
Now, be a better person,

597
43:46.229 --> 43:49.482
and when you meet someone new, don't hurt her like you hurt me.

598
43:49.565 --> 43:51.776
I hope you find love and happiness. All the best.

599
43:53.069 --> 43:54.362
[sighs] Uh, but...

600
43:55.154 --> 43:56.572
What are you two talking about?

601
43:58.241 --> 43:59.283
Nothing.

602
44:01.577 --> 44:02.662
Bye, Professor.

603
44:16.759 --> 44:19.762
PROFESSOR'S OFFICE

604
44:28.145 --> 44:31.148
PARK MINJAE PROFESSOR'S OFFICE

605
44:43.536 --> 44:45.538
[♪ pensive music playing]

606
45:10.980 --> 45:12.064
[sighs]

607
46:12.291 --> 46:13.751
[groans softly]

608
46:26.889 --> 46:28.224
[phone vibrates]

609
46:33.104 --> 46:34.772
[Jihoon] What are you doing after work today?

610
46:40.903 --> 46:42.113
[Youjin] Going home.

611
46:45.825 --> 46:47.159
[Jihoon] Want to grab dinner together?

612
46:57.294 --> 46:59.130
[Youjin] Too tired. Got to go home and sleep.

613
47:21.986 --> 47:22.987
[camera clicks]

614
47:33.789 --> 47:34.790
[scoffs]

615
47:40.921 --> 47:42.089
[door opens]

616
47:43.007 --> 47:44.008
[sighs]

617
47:44.091 --> 47:45.092
[door closes]

618
47:52.975 --> 47:54.101
Where did everyone go?

619
47:55.019 --> 47:56.103
Oh.

620
47:56.187 --> 47:59.023
Professor Park Minjae's office. They're having a meeting.

621
47:59.690 --> 48:02.818
What? They should've told me about it. Why didn't they say anything?

622
48:05.279 --> 48:06.572
[Sejin sighs]

623
48:18.125 --> 48:19.585
Aren't you going to the meeting?

624
48:21.462 --> 48:23.088
It's not a real meeting.

625
48:23.172 --> 48:25.716
They're just hanging out and chatting.

626
48:26.634 --> 48:27.635
[sighing]

627
48:28.385 --> 48:29.637
It's not a meeting.

628
48:31.597 --> 48:32.598
Hey,

629
48:33.140 --> 48:34.892
even so, this isn't right.

630
48:35.351 --> 48:37.144
We should all be chatting together.

631
48:37.228 --> 48:39.104
We're all in the same lab, aren't we?

632
48:39.855 --> 48:42.316
-Don't you know what teamwork is? -[sighs]

633
48:42.399 --> 48:44.026
Since when is hanging out teamwork?

634
48:44.109 --> 48:45.778
When we hang out, we stick together.

635
48:45.861 --> 48:48.072
We look out for each other. That's family.

636
48:51.825 --> 48:52.826
You see,

637
48:54.495 --> 48:56.247
I've always wanted to say this to you.

638
48:58.499 --> 49:01.627
Do you know how easy they go on you because you're the only girl?

639
49:01.710 --> 49:04.338
Hey, have I ever asked them to go easy on me?

640
49:04.421 --> 49:05.714
There you go again.

641
49:07.299 --> 49:09.260
The guys just accepted that you're different

642
49:09.343 --> 49:11.136
and treated you with care and respect

643
49:11.220 --> 49:13.389
as their junior and colleague. And you say what?

644
49:13.472 --> 49:15.474
"When did I ever ask them to go easy on me?"

645
49:17.017 --> 49:18.227
Go ahead, argue with me.

646
49:18.310 --> 49:19.353
Am I wrong?

647
49:20.312 --> 49:21.814
Hey, that's not what it is.

648
49:21.897 --> 49:22.898
Then what is it?

649
49:23.899 --> 49:24.900
[sighs]

650
49:26.527 --> 49:29.822
Well, obviously, I'm uncomfortable around Professor Park Minjae.

651
49:34.535 --> 49:36.453
If you're uncomfortable,

652
49:37.121 --> 49:38.122
then sit up straight.

653
49:38.664 --> 49:39.665
What?

654
49:39.748 --> 49:41.125
You think he's comfortable?

655
49:41.208 --> 49:43.377
He's uncomfortable too, but he's trying.

656
49:44.336 --> 49:47.965
Or why don't you just... just come clean?

657
49:48.048 --> 49:50.509
Say, "We secretly dated and broke up, so it's awkward."

658
49:50.593 --> 49:51.969
Why don't you just do that?

659
49:54.305 --> 49:55.306
[sighs]

660
49:55.389 --> 49:57.266
If you can't,

661
49:57.349 --> 49:58.475
don't make it obvious.

662
49:59.476 --> 50:00.853
If you're uncomfortable,

663
50:01.937 --> 50:02.938
deal with it.

664
50:15.284 --> 50:16.577
[door opens]

665
50:17.786 --> 50:18.787
[door closes]

666
50:26.503 --> 50:27.504
[knocking at door]

667
50:27.588 --> 50:28.589
Yes?

668
50:29.590 --> 50:30.633
Hey, come in.

669
50:31.258 --> 50:33.469
I heard we were having a meeting here.

670
50:33.552 --> 50:34.803
[Minjae] Yeah. Come in.

671
50:35.429 --> 50:38.140
[Taeho] We're throwing a welcome-back party for Minjae today.

672
50:38.223 --> 50:39.642
What should we eat?

673
50:40.309 --> 50:41.560
[Sejin] Oh.

674
50:41.644 --> 50:44.021
So this meeting's about what we're having for dinner?

675
50:44.104 --> 50:45.147
Exactly.

676
50:46.106 --> 50:47.608
What should we have?

677
50:47.691 --> 50:49.485
Maybe pork belly? Maybe not.

678
50:50.778 --> 50:54.490
How about beef instead of pork? It's been a while.

679
50:54.573 --> 50:55.824
Beef sounds great.

680
50:55.908 --> 50:58.994
Sirloin, tenderloin, skirt steak, brisket. Right?

681
51:00.621 --> 51:03.916
Minjae is paying, so let's get beef short ribs.

682
51:04.458 --> 51:06.251
-[Minjae scoffs] -Yeah, beef short ribs.

683
51:06.335 --> 51:07.920
Beef short ribs? As if.

684
51:08.003 --> 51:11.048
Sejin, let's go with whatever you want. It's on me.

685
51:11.131 --> 51:13.842
Oh. Then I'd say...

686
51:15.511 --> 51:16.512
Yeah?

687
51:17.596 --> 51:19.139
Fried chicken.

688
51:19.223 --> 51:20.724
Fried chicken sounds great.

689
51:20.808 --> 51:23.143
That's my junior. Those guys are all strangers.

690
51:23.227 --> 51:25.521
You're the only one I consider my brother. Thanks.

691
51:25.604 --> 51:27.690
All right, let's go with fried chicken.

692
51:27.773 --> 51:29.108
-Sejin, give me a hand? -Sure.

693
51:29.191 --> 51:30.192
Yeah. All right.

694
51:30.567 --> 51:31.652
[indistinct conversation]

695
51:31.735 --> 51:32.861
I'd love a draft beer.

696
51:37.908 --> 51:39.827
Did you book a table at the chicken place?

697
51:39.910 --> 51:42.329
Yeah, at Lulu Chicken, for six people.

698
51:42.413 --> 51:44.248
I wanted to have some beef.

699
51:46.083 --> 51:48.502
[Youjin] Oh? Are we going home already?

700
51:49.128 --> 51:51.255
No, not going home. We're having a team dinner.

701
51:51.338 --> 51:53.132
We're throwing the welcome-back party for Minjae today.

702
51:54.133 --> 51:55.134
Why?

703
51:56.051 --> 51:57.803
[Youjin] But I already have plans tonight.

704
51:59.638 --> 52:00.639
Really?

705
52:02.266 --> 52:04.643
What plans? Can't you cancel them?

706
52:04.727 --> 52:07.396
It's Minjae's welcome-back party. It'd be nice if you came.

707
52:07.479 --> 52:10.607
Yeah, join us. It's Minjae's first team dinner back.

708
52:11.525 --> 52:14.194
It's okay. If she can't make it, she can't make it.

709
52:14.278 --> 52:16.071
Yeah. It's okay. Don't worry about it.

710
52:17.364 --> 52:19.241
But, Youjin,

711
52:20.284 --> 52:22.453
just send Minjae a quick text, okay?

712
52:22.536 --> 52:25.789
Tell him you're sorry you missed his party and you'll see him next time.

713
52:25.873 --> 52:26.957
-[Youjin] I will. -[Taeho] Good.

714
52:28.041 --> 52:29.334
-Bye. -Bye.

715
52:29.418 --> 52:30.669
-Bye. -Yeah.

716
52:31.920 --> 52:33.505
-Bye, Youjin. -Good luck.

717
52:36.383 --> 52:37.426
[door opens]

718
52:43.474 --> 52:44.892
[door closes]

719
52:48.145 --> 52:49.730
[sighs] Done.

720
52:52.649 --> 52:53.650
[grunts]

721
53:08.540 --> 53:11.335
-[door lock activates] -[phone vibrates]

722
53:15.839 --> 53:18.425
[Youjin] I don't think I can join the welcome-back party today.

723
53:18.509 --> 53:19.551
I'm sorry.

724
53:21.303 --> 53:22.304
[sighs]

725
53:22.387 --> 53:23.555
[phone vibrates]

726
53:26.099 --> 53:28.352
[Youjin] Welcome back.

727
53:30.521 --> 53:32.022
[huffs]

728
53:37.402 --> 53:39.404
[indistinct conversation]

729
53:41.532 --> 53:42.866
[phone vibrates]

730
53:49.456 --> 53:51.792
[Minjae] Okay. Thanks.

731
53:51.875 --> 53:52.960
I'll see you around.

732
54:04.763 --> 54:06.431
[♪ classical music playing over speakers]

733
54:06.515 --> 54:07.975
-Hello. -Hello.

734
54:08.058 --> 54:10.894
Hi, I have a reservation for two under the name Lee Jihoon.

735
54:10.978 --> 54:13.480
All right. Let me show you to your table.

736
54:13.564 --> 54:14.565
Okay.

737
54:20.320 --> 54:21.530
Here's your table.

738
54:21.613 --> 54:22.614
Thanks.

739
54:23.991 --> 54:25.951
May I take your bag and coat?

740
54:26.034 --> 54:28.662
Uh... I'll keep my bag. Just the coat, please.

741
54:28.787 --> 54:29.788
Of course. Got it.

742
54:29.872 --> 54:30.873
Thank you.

743
54:31.498 --> 54:32.666
-Thank you. -No problem.

744
55:00.235 --> 55:02.362
[♪ lively music playing over speakers]

745
55:04.906 --> 55:06.033
All right. [clears throat]

746
55:06.116 --> 55:07.784
Now that we've all had a few bites...

747
55:09.453 --> 55:13.415
The pride of our lab and my soulmate!

748
55:13.498 --> 55:14.583
[chuckles]

749
55:14.666 --> 55:18.337
Let's welcome Professor Park Minjae on his triumphant return.

750
55:18.420 --> 55:20.881
Now, a round of applause.

751
55:20.964 --> 55:22.215
Welcome back.

752
55:22.299 --> 55:23.300
Thanks.

753
55:24.426 --> 55:29.056
All right. Now, let's hear a few words from Professor Park.

754
55:29.139 --> 55:31.308
But before that, um...

755
55:31.391 --> 55:34.394
since he's come back from the States,

756
55:34.478 --> 55:38.398
we'll have him give his speech in English,

757
55:39.608 --> 55:41.276
which he's more comfortable with.

758
55:41.360 --> 55:43.570
-Jeez. -[in English] Here you are. [laughs]

759
55:44.279 --> 55:45.447
[Hangyeol in Korean] Let's hear it.

760
55:46.865 --> 55:47.949
[in English] Okay.

761
55:48.033 --> 55:49.368
Uh...

762
55:49.451 --> 55:51.161
Thank you, everyone.

763
55:51.953 --> 55:53.413
Uh...

764
55:53.497 --> 55:55.123
I love you. Okay.

765
55:55.207 --> 55:56.958
-[in Korean] Bravo. All right. -Youjin.

766
55:57.042 --> 55:58.377
Hey, Youjin.

767
55:59.252 --> 56:00.253
Huh?

768
56:00.337 --> 56:02.923
-You had plans. How did you make it? -You made it.

769
56:03.674 --> 56:05.258
I pushed my plans back a bit.

770
56:06.134 --> 56:08.512
It's Minjae's party. I should at least stop by.

771
56:08.595 --> 56:09.596
[exclaims]

772
56:10.347 --> 56:14.351
Our Youjin is so polite, right?

773
56:14.434 --> 56:17.896
She knows how to show respect to her seniors. [laughs]

774
56:17.979 --> 56:19.690
-Yeah. -Eat up.

775
56:19.773 --> 56:22.067
-Excuse me. Could we... -I'm sitting up straight now.

776
56:22.150 --> 56:23.151
[Chansoo] Huh?

777
56:23.735 --> 56:25.779
Could we get a small plate, please?

778
56:25.862 --> 56:28.490
Minjae, welcome back to Korea.

779
56:30.033 --> 56:31.034
Thanks.

780
56:33.578 --> 56:35.956
[♪ soft piano music playing over speakers]

781
56:49.428 --> 56:51.555
-Let me refill your glass. -Yes, thank you.

782
57:08.697 --> 57:09.698
Youjin.

783
57:10.866 --> 57:12.743
Let me walk you to the bus stop.

784
57:12.826 --> 57:15.412
It's okay. I'm going to take a taxi because it's late.

785
57:15.495 --> 57:17.205
A taxi? Then let me get one for you.

786
57:17.289 --> 57:19.499
No, I'm fine. I can do it.

787
57:19.583 --> 57:21.543
No, you're late because of me.

788
57:21.626 --> 57:22.878
Come on, follow me.

789
57:26.965 --> 57:28.842
Are you meeting Professor Lee Jihoon?

790
57:30.302 --> 57:31.303
Yes.

791
57:32.888 --> 57:34.890
Is he nice to you?

792
57:37.267 --> 57:38.769
Yeah, I guess.

793
57:41.146 --> 57:42.522
He seems like a nice guy.

794
57:44.399 --> 57:46.359
He is. And he's really smart.

795
57:47.068 --> 57:48.069
And sexy?

796
57:49.112 --> 57:50.113
What?

797
57:50.739 --> 57:52.449
Well, Kim Sejin said

798
57:52.532 --> 57:55.202
Professor Lee is popular with girls because he's sexy.

799
57:55.744 --> 57:57.871
Oh... As if.

800
57:57.954 --> 57:59.539
[chuckles]

801
58:01.374 --> 58:05.212
He's so full of himself, and he says such mean things.

802
58:06.463 --> 58:08.924
He said Professor Lee is popular with girls?

803
58:09.007 --> 58:10.217
Yeah.

804
58:10.300 --> 58:13.136
But there must be something you find attractive about him

805
58:13.220 --> 58:14.554
if you're dating him.

806
58:15.806 --> 58:16.807
What?

807
58:17.516 --> 58:19.935
Who said I was dating him?

808
58:21.436 --> 58:22.562
-Huh? -What crazy asshole

809
58:22.646 --> 58:23.855
is going around saying that?

810
58:27.609 --> 58:29.778
So, it's not true?

811
58:31.029 --> 58:32.405
Don't be ridiculous.

812
58:38.912 --> 58:42.415
If you're not marrying him or seeing him,

813
58:45.126 --> 58:46.962
can we get back together?

814
58:49.130 --> 58:50.131
No.

815
58:51.550 --> 58:55.262
Even if I beg you to forgive me and promise I'll never do it again?

816
58:57.472 --> 58:58.473
No.

817
59:01.518 --> 59:05.397
I'm not making excuses, but I really was sick.

818
59:05.480 --> 59:08.108
Back then, I honestly thought I might die.

819
59:08.191 --> 59:11.236
You don't know because I never told you what was going on...

820
59:11.319 --> 59:12.320
I know.

821
59:13.488 --> 59:15.657
It must've been so painful and hard for you.

822
59:16.658 --> 59:18.618
You were probably so overwhelmed

823
59:18.702 --> 59:20.871
that you couldn't think about anything else.

824
59:21.955 --> 59:24.291
You were sick. How could you think of anyone else?

825
59:24.374 --> 59:26.293
No, that's not what it was like!

826
59:26.376 --> 59:27.752
Don't yell at me.

827
59:31.006 --> 59:33.967
Whether I was too much, things were too hard, whatever the reason,

828
59:35.552 --> 59:36.553
you left me once.

829
59:36.636 --> 59:38.138
How do I know it won't happen again?

830
59:38.221 --> 59:40.432
[yelling] No, I said that's not it!

831
59:40.515 --> 59:42.601
[yelling] I told you not to yell at me!

832
59:42.684 --> 59:44.811
[whimpers]

833
59:46.229 --> 59:48.148
All right. I... Don't cry. Come here.

834
59:48.231 --> 59:50.066
That was my bad. I'm sorry. I...

835
59:51.484 --> 59:53.403
I'm sorry. Don't cry, okay?

836
01:00:07.292 --> 01:00:09.669
But can you try to understand me too?

837
01:00:11.171 --> 01:00:13.924
I'm a coward, and I always overthink everything.

838
01:00:14.007 --> 01:00:16.426
I always imagine the worst.

839
01:00:18.637 --> 01:00:19.679
I really...

840
01:00:20.889 --> 01:00:23.433
I really thought I was going to die back then.

841
01:00:24.351 --> 01:00:25.352
That's why...

842
01:00:27.812 --> 01:00:30.106
I didn't want to make things hard for you.

843
01:00:30.190 --> 01:00:32.317
That's why I wanted to let you go.

844
01:00:32.400 --> 01:00:34.486
I don't want to hear any of that bullshit.

845
01:00:35.612 --> 01:00:38.031
You think you were the only one having a hard time?

846
01:00:38.114 --> 01:00:39.824
You think you were the only one?

847
01:00:41.451 --> 01:00:44.120
I almost died back then too. I did too.

848
01:00:45.038 --> 01:00:46.831
I thought I'd rather die

849
01:00:47.332 --> 01:00:48.833
than break up with you.

850
01:00:48.917 --> 01:00:50.543
That's what I thought!

851
01:00:52.128 --> 01:00:55.715
You didn't die, but I died back then!

852
01:00:58.385 --> 01:01:00.679
So how am I supposed to forgive you?

853
01:01:01.304 --> 01:01:04.140
How am I supposed to take you back? How?

854
01:01:13.900 --> 01:01:15.777
My answer is no, and that's final.

855
01:01:19.781 --> 01:01:21.783
[♪ gentle song playing]

856
01:02:53.708 --> 01:02:57.629
BETWEEN STEPS

857
01:02:57.712 --> 01:03:01.174
[Youjin] I don't want any weird rumors to start about you because of me.

858
01:03:01.257 --> 01:03:02.675
I already like someone.

859
01:03:02.759 --> 01:03:05.929
I gave you my whole heart, my everything.

860
01:03:06.012 --> 01:03:08.181
But you betrayed it and just threw it away.

861
01:03:08.264 --> 01:03:10.683
[Minjae] Being with you made me happy,

862
01:03:10.767 --> 01:03:13.228
but it also really scared me.

863
01:03:14.604 --> 01:03:17.148
I was scared that one day, it'd all end.

864
01:03:18.108 --> 01:03:19.651
And that I'd be abandoned.

865
01:03:20.610 --> 01:03:22.779
You loved me,

866
01:03:22.862 --> 01:03:24.155
but I didn't.
